From 4487e0fa3b1033bc865bdcecefd8da96760db0ec Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 04:20:28 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat(browser): lease every built-in browser tool under
 browser.managed_agent [daveey]

browser_exec was the only managed-Chrome client that acquired an owner lease; the
built-in tools (navigate/snapshot/click/..., browser_cdp, browser_dialog, the vault
page ops) resolved the raw cdp_url, which the managed supervisor answers with 403.

- browser_agent_lifecycle: tool_lease (task-scoped "tools" owner, nested reuse,
  no harness daemon), scoped_override (raises outside a lease, never the raw
  root), renew_selected (vault keeps the last-selected exec/tools scope leased;
  a rotated capability fails clearly).
- _get_cdp_override resolves through the lease; agent-browser sessions pin their
  lease and re-attach on rotation; managed close is a no-op so cleanup never
  wakes Chrome; Lightpanda Chrome fallback gated off for managed sessions.
- Unmanaged cdp_url behavior unchanged (tests run every path both ways).
